  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe are minimizing the penalty function defined by the ratio of twice the sequence length and the maximum convolution value divided by the squared sum of the sequence. The approach will be to systematically explore sequences of varying lengths, starting from shorter sequences and gradually increasing length as time permits. This ensures we capitalize on the tradeoffs typically observed at borderline lengths between 500 and 1000, where the normalized penalty is often minimized. We will use a combination of initializations, linear programs and subgradient steps to optimize each sequence length, with careful time budgeting to maintain feasibility.\n\nMathematical specification:\nFor each sequence length n, we generate a normalized candidate (sum=1) and the objective is obj = 2*n*max(convolve(a,a,mode=\"full\")) / (sum(a))^2. The optimization process consists of:\n1. Initial candidate generation via `random_init` function\n2. Quick subgradient steps (`subgradient_optimize`) to adjust the sequence\n3. Main alternating-LP phase (`alternating_lp`) to refine the sequence\n4. Advanced polishing phase (`polish_sequence`) to further reduce the objective\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Read parent sequence and initialize best candidate storage\n2. Define set of sequence lengths to explore, with highest priority given to parent's length (100) and a few surrounding values\n3. For each n in the sorted list:\n   - Allocate time proportionally (prioritize shorter sequences first)\n   - Generate initial sequence using `random_init`\n   - Apply quick subgradient optimization\n   - Run alternating LP/line search optimization\n   - Perform intensive polishing cycles\n   - Check for fallback conditions if needed\n4. Maintain best candidate throughout the process and return it\n\nSearch choices and variations:\nWe\u63a2\u7d22\u5e8f\u5217\u957f\u5ea6n\u4ece50\u52301500\uff0c\u4e3b\u8981\u4f7f\u7528\u4ee5\u4e0b\u521d\u59cb\u5316\u65b9\u6cd5\uff1a\n- \u5b9a\u671f\u4f7f\u7528\u4e0d\u540cn\u503c\u5468\u56f4\u7684\u5e8f\u5217\u957f\u5ea6\n- \u591a\u8f6e\u4f18\u5316\u4e2d\u5c1d\u8bd5\u4e0d\u540c\u7684tau_s\u53c2\u6570\u914d\u7f6e\n- \u5f53\u5e8f\u5217\u957f\u5ea6\u8f83\u5927\u65f6\u4f7f\u7528\u66f4\u7ecf\u6d4e\u7684\u4f18\u5316\u7b56\u7565\n\nComputation budget and robustness:\nAllocate 15 seconds per initial sequence generation, 60 seconds for primary optimization, and 30 seconds for polishing. Total time budget is 1500 seconds. Implement 3 phases of optimization and multiple reinitialization strategies.\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Always check feasibility before returning candidate\n- Ensure \u6210\u7ee9 is computed exactly using the provided evaluate_sequence function\n- Maintain best candidate from all explored lengths\n- Fallback to uniform distribution if needed",
